<!--
  Themed-icon MONOCHROME layer (API 33+). The system tints this flat; only the silhouette
  carries meaning, so it is a single evenOdd path: the cross slab with all 33 cells
  punched out.

  Chosen variant: ALL 33 holes, not the centre-hole-only alternative. A cross with one dot
  does not read as a peg board; the perforated cross does.

  Hole radius is 15 here rather than the 20 used on the colour foreground. At 0.55 scale a
  20-unit hole leaves only about 2.3dp of webbing between neighbours, which turns to mush
  under a single flat tint; 15 leaves 56 - 30 = 26 units, roughly 3.8dp. The centre hole
  stays at radius 20 so the "one empty cell" read survives.
-->
